      "markdown": "## Cramer's Rule for Linear Systems of Three Equations \n\n(5)\n\nis \n\n(6)\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}&a_{_{11}}x_{_{1}}+a_{_{12}}x_{_{2}}+a_{_{13}}x_{_{3}}=b_{_{1}}\\\\&a_{_{21}}x_{_{1}}+a_{_{22}}x_{_{2}}+a_{_{23}}x_{_{3}}=b_{_{2}}\\\\&a_{_{31}}x_{_{1}}+a_{_{32}}x_{_{2}}+a_{_{33}}x_{_{3}}=b_{_{3}}\\\\ \\end{aligned}$$\n\n$$x_{_{1}}=\\frac{D_{_{1}}}{D},\\quad x_{_{2}}=\\frac{D_{_{2}}}{D},\\quad x_{_{3}}=\\frac{D_{_{3}}}{D}with the determinantD o the system iven by (4) and $$\n\n(D≠0)\n\nwith the determinantD o the system iven by (4) and \n\n$$D_{1}=\\begin{vmatrix}b_{1}&a_{12}&a_{13}\\\\ b_{2}&a_{22}&a_{23}\\\\ b_{3}&a_{32}&a_{33}\\end{vmatrix},\\quad D_{2}=\\begin{vmatrix}a_{11}&b_{1}&a_{13}\\\\ a_{21}&b_{2}&a_{23}\\\\ a_{31}&b_{3}&a_{33}\\end{vmatrix},\\quad D_{3}=\\begin{vmatrix}a_{11}&a_{12}&b_{1}\\\\ a_{21}&a_{22}&b_{2}\\\\ a_{31}&a_{32}&b_{3}\\end{vmatrix}.$$\n\nNote that $D_{1},D_{2},D_{3}$ are obtained by replacing gColumns s 1, 2,$3,$ respectively, by the column of the right sides of (5).",
